My gut says the medical photos would make me roll my eyes, and the "excess calories cause obesity" wording sounds like a lecture. A number on the packet is different: I'd glance at it when I'm stood there with a Dairy Milk in one hand and a fruit pot in the other, though money would still matter more to me than either.

Scheme D comes closest to something I'd actually use. Scheme C gets some points for the calorie badge, but I'd likely ignore the scary picture. The text-only warnings get less, because I'd read them as nagging and skip past.

